* UMIST Database for Astrochemistry 2012
*
* Isotopomeres included by M.Roellig, 2013
* Reactions with negative gammas have been re-fitted
* new branching ratios from Chabot et al. 2013 applied
* UMIST only included c-C3H, c-C3H2, c-C3H2+, and c-C3H3+, we added also the l- forms
* for convenience the "l-" isomer is indicated by a leading "l" , the "c-" isomer by a leading "c"
* e.g. c-C3H -> cC3H, ....
* 2021: activated JH2
* Version 1.4
*******************************************************************************************************************
* The following reactions are provided with multiple temperature regimes. I consistently picked the lower temp range. This has to be validated at some point.
