******* NOTE: THE REACTION RATES CAN BE FOUND IN
******* LANGER, GRAEDEL, FRERKING, ARMENTROUT, 1984, APJ 277, 581, (LGFA) FOR DIFFERENT TEPERATURES
******* THE PARAMETERS GIVEN HERE WERE DERIVED FROM THOSE IN LANGER ET AL (1984), USING
******* THE KNOWN ZERO-POINT ENERGY DIFFERENCE (PARAMTETER K3=DELTA E) AND USING THE
******* USUAL PARAMTERISATION OF K = K1 (T/300)^K2 EXP(-K3/T) WHERE K3=0 FOR THE
******* REACTION, AND K3=DELTA E FOR THE BACK REACTION.
******* USE THE K3 = DELTA E IN TABLE 1 OF LANGER ET AL (1984)
******* FRANK BENSCH 8.6.2001
******* (NOTE, THAT IN MAIK'S CODE, THE RATE IN TAB 3 OF LANGER ARE USED AS LUT,
******* INTERPOLATING BETWEEN THEM IF NEEDED, WHILE HERE WE USE THE PARAMTERISATION
******* OF THE REACTION RATES WITH THE CONSTANTS K1, K2, K3)
******* Markus Roellig, 23.11.2008 ***************************************************
