*                                                                                                                 *
*                                                                                                                 *
*                                              GRAIN CHEMISTRY                                                    *
*                                                                                                                 *
*                                                                                                                 *
*******************************************************************************************************************
* THERMAL DESORPTION REACTIONS                                                               E_desor   H2des_eff mass
* each desorption process has to be activated with a reaction entry of the following form:
*   xxxx JH              EVAP            H                                                   3.50E+02  0.01      1.0
* EVAP denotes thermal desorption. The following parameters are supplied:
*         E_desorb     is the binding energy of the grain species (denoted by a prepend "J" in Kelvin
*         H2des_eff    is the efficiency epsilon for the H2 formation induced desorption (see Eq(5) from
*                      Willacy, Rawlings, and Williams, 1994, MNRAS, 269, 921-927
*                      this is an arbitrary parameter ( < 1 ). When set to 0 it deactivates this process for this
*                      species (default=0.01, set 0.00 to switch off)
*         mass         is the mass of the surface species in units of the hydrogen mass
*
* DIRECT COSMIC RAY DESORPTION
* this process is automatically added for each thermal desorption process. It covers the direct hit of a grain
* by a Fe nucleus from CR and the subsequent (explosive) grain heating. This allows to desorp some species even
* if the grain temperature is very low. We use EQ(63) from Woitke et al. 2009)
*
*******************************************************************************************************************
* GRAIN ACCRETION REACTION
* each accretion process has to be activated by a reaction entry of the following form:
*                                                                                                               mass
*   5024 CO              GRAIN           JCO                                                 0.00E-00  0.00     28.0
* GRAIN denotes accretion. The following parameters have to be supplied:
*         mass         is the mass of the surface species in units of the hydrogen mass
*
*******************************************************************************************************************
* PHOTO-DESORPTION REACTION
* We use EQ(62) from Woitke et al 2009
* each photo-desorption process has to be activated by a reaction entry of the following form:
*                                                                                            yield               gamma
*   5022 JCO             PHDES           CO                                                  2.70E-03  0.00      1.8
* PHDES denotes photo-desorption. The following parameters have to be supplied:
*         yield         is the photo-desorption yield (per UV PHOTON) of the surface species taken from
*                       Woitke et al. 2009, A&A 501, 383-406 and Willacy, Rawlings, and Williams, 1994, MNRAS, 269, 921-927
*         gamma         is the photo-attenuation parameter similar to other photo-reactions.
*
*  NOT USED: Assuming that JCO dissociates like CO (scaled with 0.01 because of only that fraction is sitting at the surface)
** NOT USED: Assuming a Photodesorption rate of 10^8 * Yield* surface fraction* local UV field (Hollenbach et al. 2009)
*
*  COSMIC RAY INDUCED PHOTODESORPTION: Willacy, Rawlings & Williams 1994, MNRAS 269,921
*
*    R=F_p*Y*<sigma_Dust>*n_H*COSRAY/1.3e-17*n_S(I)/(Sum of all dust species)
*    yield Y = 0.1 PHOTONs^-1
*    PHOTON Flux = 1.5D+4 PHOTONs/cm^2/s (full formula from Cecchi-Pestellini & Aiello 1992 for later implementation)
*                                      = 960(1/(1-w))(zeta/1.e-17)(N_H/A_V/(1.e21))(R_V/3.2)^1.5
*                -> gamma= 0.1*1.5d4/2 =750.0   (2 will be multiplied to it again in CMREAD.F)
*
*
* H2 induced desorption is covered with the EVAP reaction
*
*
* First we have a set of 4 reactions per species covering accretion and desorption
* Please note, that photo-desorption yields (1st parameter) is basically unknown except for a small number of species
* We assume a default value of 1.0e-3. Alternatively one could remove the "PHDES" lines to deactivate the photo-desorption
*
***************************************************************************************************************************
**         H
***************************************************************************************************************************
   7000 H               GRAIN           JH                                                  0.00E+00  0.00      1.0   9 999
